test_command=for t in tests/*_test.sh; do sh "$t" || exit 1; done
id=repodocs-01 result=green reason=unit test "repodocs-01: the spdd/ Structure bullet in AGENTS.md states the real state (the three directories exist in the checkout; changes holds in-flight changes empty between flows, specs the governing per-domain specs, archive the archived changes) and keeps the specifier/verifier ownership, with no absent-or-created-on-first-run claim" in tests/repodocs_test.sh passes (the single bullet extracted from AGENTS.md's ## Structure section carries "exist in the checkout", "in-flight changes", "empty between flows", "governing per-domain spec", "archived changes", "specifier creates `spdd/changes/<slug>/`", "verifier creates/updates `spdd/specs/`", "moves approved changes to `spdd/archive/`", and refuses "not present yet"/"created on first run"; red before the line-13 correction, green after)
id=repodocs-02 result=green reason=unit test "repodocs-02: the corrected spdd/ Structure bullet is byte-for-byte identical between AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md" in tests/repodocs_test.sh passes (cmp of the two Structure-scoped bullet extracts; the test also refuses the stale "not present yet" in either copy, so two identical stale pre-fix bullets -- the base state -- cannot pass it; green after the identical correction was applied to both docs' line 13)
id=repodocs-03 result=green reason=unit test "repodocs-03: neither AGENTS.md nor CLAUDE.md anywhere says the spdd/ directories are 'not present yet', created on first run, or otherwise not yet existing, while the out-of-scope Overview 'No application code lives here yet' sentence survives untouched" in tests/repodocs_test.sh passes (whole-file refusals of both phrases plus an spdd/-line non-existence regex scan hitting only the corrected line pre-fix and nothing post-fix -- verified no false positives on the docs' other spdd/-mentioning lines -- and a pin that the out-of-scope Overview sentence is still present in both files)
